column1:
2:3|Fire devours ahead of them;
flame burns behind them.
Before them the land is like the garden of Eden;
behind them, a desolate wilderness.
Nothing escapes them.|Maintains before/behind pattern and Eden comparison.

2:16|Gather the people;
set apart the congregation.
Assemble the elders;
gather children and nursing infants.
Let the bridegroom leave his room
and the bride her wedding chamber.|Retains all ages and both newlyweds rather than only general everyone language.

2:28|Afterward I will pour out my Spirit on all flesh.
Your sons and daughters will prophesy;
your old men will dream dreams;
your young men will see visions.|Keeps all flesh, both sexes in prophecy, and age-specific dream/vision language.
